> Could it be because the qualifier definition has `@Target({ FIELD, TYPE, PARAMETER })` instead of ` @Target({METHOD, FIELD, PARAMETER, TYPE})`?

That sounds... strange?

@eAybars I'm interested in that reproducer. In particular, can you turn it into a test inside the extension, next to `ElasticsearchClientConfigTest`? It's really surprising that `ElasticsearchClientConfigTest` passes if user beans are ignored.

No need for a reproducer. AFAICS the test is only working because we inject the class itself to test it. If I remove
```
    @Inject
    @ElasticsearchClientConfig
    TestConfigurator testConfigurator;
```
the configurator is not executed.
